                  <zone forceUpdate='true' h='24530' id='20' type-v2='text' w='44508' x='44991' y='74530'>
                    <formatted-text>
                      <run bold='true' fontsize='9'>  KEY INSIGHTS</run>
                      <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
                      <run fontalignment='0' fontsize='9'>  • Asia improved most: life expectancy rose from 46.3 (1952) to 70.7 years (2007), +24.4 years.</run>
                      <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
                      <run fontalignment='0' fontsize='9'>  • Africa remains lowest at 54.8 years in 2007; progress stalled between 1987 and 2002.</run>
                      <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
                      <run fontalignment='0' fontsize='9'>  • 25 of 142 countries are High Priority in 2007 - 24 of them in Africa.</run>
                      <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
                      <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                      <run fontsize='9'>Æ </run>
                      <run bold='true' fontsize='9'> RECOMMENDATION</run>
                      <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
                      <run fontalignment='0' fontsize='9'>Prioritise deeper policy review in Sub-Saharan Africa, where 24 of 25 High Priority countries are located and life expectancy is 12 years below the world average (67.0). Note: data ends in 2007.</run>
                    </formatted-text>
